<title>POLAND: Polish livestock numbers rise in April vs December.</title>
<headline>Polish livestock numbers rise in April vs December.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The headcount for Polish pigs and cattle increased by 1.2 and 4.7 percent respectively in April from last December, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said in a report released on Monday.</p>
<p>GUS said, however, that the number of pigs on farms fell 9.0 percent against April 1996 to last month's 17.91 million.</p>
<p>The number of cattle on farms fell by 1.7 percent from the corresponding month last year to April's 7.28 million.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
